1
00:00:00,544 --> 00:00:04,964
(Penny(in hallway):)Okay, you guys, look, I know this is none
of my business, but I just... I have to ask.

2
00:00:05,132 --> 00:00:06,882
(Penny(in hallway):)What's Sheldon's deal?

3
00:00:10,429 --> 00:00:13,559
- What do you mean, "deal"?
- You know, like, what's his deal?

4
00:00:13,724 --> 00:00:16,894
(Penny:)Is it girls? Guys? Sock puppets?

5
00:00:17,561 --> 00:00:22,111
(Leonard:)Honestly, we've been operating
under the assumption that he has no deal.

6
00:00:22,274 --> 00:00:24,944
- Oh, come on, everybody has a deal.
- Not Sheldon.

7
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:29,660
(Howard:)Over the years, we've formulated many
theories about how he might reproduce.

8
00:00:30,866 --> 00:00:33,746
I'm an advocate of mitosis.

9
00:00:34,703 --> 00:00:36,033
(Penny:)I'm sorry?

10
00:00:36,205 --> 00:00:39,455
(Howard:)I believe, one day, Sheldon will eat
an enormous amount of Thai food...

11
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:42,665
(Howard:)...and split into two Sheldons.

12
00:00:44,004 --> 00:00:47,544
(Leonard:)On the other hand, I think Sheldon
might be the larval form of his species.

13
00:00:47,716 --> 00:00:49,966
(Leonard:)He'll spin a cocoon
and emerge two months later...

14
00:00:50,135 --> 00:00:52,595
(Leonard:)...with moth wings and an exoskeleton.

15
00:00:53,764 --> 00:00:58,024
(Penny:)Okay, well, thanks for the nightmares.

